{"kind":"assert","text":"R2 source reconnaissance identifies a shared eager ScopeObject SQL bootstrap and a separate hosted-registry bootstrap. A known-ID gate plus lazy first-genesis initialization is the smallest complete architectural direction found; lazy CREATE TABLE alone is incomplete. Existing-namespace proof-index migration and the zero-SQL target-versus-index scope require planner confirmation. No implementation, runtime or completion claimed.","body":{"costs":"Known-ID index: one authoritative O(1) index lookup per distinct target RPC (not a price-free cache); simple unknown HTTP/site/application usually one target check and no targetSQL; known app context additionally checks rules; foreign n target RPCs incur n checks within existing bounds; registry authority at least one membership check. Once initialized, an optional immutable positive per-instance membership memo removes repeat index reads in that activation only; no negative-cache liveness claim. Index writes O(1) per admitted scope plus rollout/backfill; cross-object publication failures need failclosed resumable ownership. Lazy-per-object marker alternative: one bounded synchronous localKV lookup per cold activation, zeroextra warm lookup; marker +genesis can share synchronous transaction. It still uses underlyingSQLite and needs legacy backfill; not a literal physical-zeroSQL shortcut. Lazytables alone: avoidsDDL but stillSELECT/PRAGMA and constructor sidecars beforeproof, so fails request as stated.","lifecycle":"Cold initialization must remain inert for readiness(), query/proof helpers, source()/observe()/siteRoom(), #first parked-operation resumption, all alarm paths and constructor signer maintenance. Known scope restart retains legitimate parked work, timed drain, dispatch/outside, signer maintenance, archive/floor earliest-wake arbitration; do not globally turn those off. First-genesis schema/fold/marker rollback together. Existing arbitrary-name schema-only objects are not verified scopes.